    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "When people think wealth management, they often think about the glitzy power cities like New York and London. Would it surprise you to find top rated wealth management somewhere like West Virginia? Well, that's where my guest today is a shining example. This is YPO 10 Minute Tips from the Toppie. I'm Kevin Dom, and each week I bring you insights from the world's top executives of YPO. All made possible with grants from Gazelle's Growth Institute, growthinstitute.com. YPO member David McKinley is an eighth-generation Appalachian, tracing his West Virginia roots back to the 1600s. David's father is a longtime representative of Northern West Virginia and the U.S. Congress, continuing a family tradition of public service that goes back 150 years. David pursued his own path in the family business of leadership, becoming a strong advocate for West Virginia and Appalachian economic opportunities. After holding positions at West Banco and Wells Fargo, David founded McKinley Carter Wealth Services, which today has over a billion dollars under management and was recently named CNBC's top 100 wealth advisors list. David also runs Willow Glen Capital, an investment portfolio of privately held businesses focused on revitalizing Appalachia. David was named to the state journal's list of who's who in West Virginia business and since 2009 has served as a governor appointed trustee of the West Virginia Investment Management Board. David, welcome to the show. Thank you. Appreciate you having me. So, 8th generation West Virginia, a family that's 150 years involved in business and politics and wealth. So, what comes with that sort of legacy responsibility? How does that impact you growing up?",
