  {
    "episode_id": 74769,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74769.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Yes. Several years ago, we spent an awful lot of time thinking about tagline, like in the heart of what we do, what is it? It's about helping our clients live a good life. And when you think about all the various concerns, the human concerns that we have, whether it be our business, our families, our financial situation, our legacies, could it be spirituality? Could it be the health, physical health, health of relationships? There's a variety of concerns and I think everybody defines success in their own way, but you need to find some appropriate blending of those concerns where I believe people fail is when they are focused So much time and energy in one area that there's not sufficient balance to lead a healthy, good life. You have great work, great financial situation, and your family's falling apart. You've lost your spirituality. The list goes on. So I think that is a key part of our focus. How do we help clients find an appropriate blend in their life? and guide them through a variety of financial decisions. And when they have enough assets to maintain their financial autonomy and potentially for generations, what new possibilities does that create for them? And that's a conversation that I don't think naturally happens among our competitors.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
